FlowWeaver is licensed in two parts, along the line between the two trees
of the library (docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, "Två träd"):

  src/editor/, src/entries/editor.ts, and the editor bundles built from them
  (flowweaver-editor.js, flowweaver-editor.global.js):
      Mozilla Public License 2.0 — see src/editor/LICENSE

  everything else — the viewer and its bundles, tokens.css, the type
  declarations, the reference host, the integrations, the documentation,
  the tooling:
      MIT — see LICENSE-MIT

Each bundle states its licence on its first line.

The viewer never contains a line from src/editor/: src/entries/entries.test.ts
follows the import graph from src/entries/viewer.ts and fails on any file
under src/editor/. So the MIT-licensed viewer bundle is MIT all the way down.

